esting 485,500,000 as a candidate. I'll compute 31,579 × 485,500 by breaking it into 31,579 × 485,000 plus 31,579 × 500. For the first part, I can calculate 31,579 × 485 as 31,579 × (500 - 15), which gives me 15,789,500 minus 473,685.\n\nThat equals 15,315,815, so 31,579 × 485,000 = 15,315,815,000. Adding 31,579 × 500 = 15,789,500 gives me 15,331,604,500 for the base calculation. Scaling up to 485,500,000 means 31,579 × 485,500,000 = 15,331,604,500,000, which exceeds the dividend, so I need a smaller quotient.\n\nTesting 485,480,000 instead: 31,579 × 485,480 = 31,579 × (485,500 - 20) = 15,331,604,500 - 631,580 = 15,330,972,920. This scales to 15,330,972,920,000, leaving a remainder of 26,831,182. From this remainder, 31,579 × 800 = 25,263,200, leaving 1,567,982. Then 31,579 × 49 = 1,578,950 - 31,579 = 1,547,371, with a final remainder of 20,611. The quotient is 485,480,849.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":28613,"cache_read_input_tokens":20965,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":28613},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"63f2ae24-fc3d-3348-008d-4127610461e3","uuid":"62e18491-9b25-4b5e-9ae2-36232d01842e"}
